ath-academy-id "q-73339" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{5}^{3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-5$, calculate\n${\\int }_{3}^{5}(5-4f(x))\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{5}^{3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factoring out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{5}(5-4f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\cdot x{|}_{3}^{5}-4(5) \\\\  & =5(5-3)-20 \\\\  & =10-20 \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73339/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff2f1a9d-2b0e-5a18-98d5-4f49f6f1527b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73339"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346213/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "99d556a4-dcc6-5cde-9fcf-6d51e44ac154" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186315679 :answer-field/choices ["q-346213/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}]
